{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof repeats append-subset transitivity and membership plumbing in every recursive case. A local append-monotonicity lemma lets the structural cases compose their induction hypotheses directly, reducing syntax and elaboration work while preserving the special normalized-old application argument.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intros Hnorm\\n  have appendSubset {a b c d : List Expression.Ident}\\n      (hac : a.Subset c) (hbd : b.Subset d) :\\n      (a ++ b).Subset (c ++ d) := by\\n    intros x hx\\n    simp only [List.mem_append] at hx ⊢\\n    exact hx.elim (fun h => Or.inl (hac h)) (fun h => Or.inr (hbd h))\\n  induction post <;>\\n    simp [Imperative.HasVarsPure.getVars, extractOldExprVars,\\n      Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars] at Hnorm ⊢ <;>\\n    try simp_all\\n  case app fn e fn_ih e_ih =>\\n    unfold extractOldExprVars\\n    split\\n    · simp [Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars]\\n      intros x hx\\n      exact hx\\n    · next Hfalse =>\\n      cases Hnorm with\\n      | app Hfn He Hold =>\\n        exfalso\\n        specialize Hold (by constructor)\\n        cases Hold\\n        exact Hfalse rfl\\n    · cases Hnorm with\\n      | app Hfn He Hold =>\\n        exact appendSubset (fn_ih Hfn) (e_ih He)\\n  case abs ih =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply ih\\n    assumption\\n  case quant trih eih =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply appendSubset\\n    · apply trih\\n      assumption\\n    · apply eih\\n      assumption\\n  case ite cih tih eih =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply appendSubset\\n    · apply cih\\n      assumption\\n    · apply appendSubset\\n      · apply tih\\n        assumption\\n      · apply eih\\n        assumption\\n  case eq ih1 ih2 =>\\n    cases Hnorm\\n    apply appendSubset\\n    · apply ih1\\n      assumption\\n    · apply ih2\\n      assumption\"}"}}
